-- title:
--   Surjectivity of Xi on points over an algebraically closed field
-- statement:
--   Work in the full Čerednik–Drinfeld frame: primes $r \neq \bar r$ and a level $N$ with $r \nmid N$; a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$, $\pi$-adically complete for an irreducible $\pi$, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$, with fraction field $K_0$; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} =$ `Onr` over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $Fr$, complete for $(\pi)$, with $(\pi)$ maximal, every element a root of a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial mod $\pi$, every monic polynomial having a root mod $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r}$ mod $\pi$; a quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ with $0 < a$ or $0 < b$ whose completion at a finite place is a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ containing $\mathbb Z$, with a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2} \times \mathbb Z_{r^2}$ satisfying the additivity, twisted multiplicativity, injectivity, density and trace conditions of `IsOrderCoord`; a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ with a height-$4$ formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ and coordinates $\theta_0$ presenting its formal group via $\mathrm{coord}$; $\iota\colon \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$; a moduli package $M$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ that is a Zariski sheaf, together with $\eta$ attaching to each rigidified object over $B$ a point of $M(B)$, such that on admissible objects over Noetherian rings $\eta$ separates precisely isomorphism classes, is natural in $B$, and is surjective after passage to some Zariski cover by admissible objects; an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$-action and of $\varpi$ on $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image agrees with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ after scaling by a fixed power of $r$; a map $\kappa\colon \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi) \to \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps, and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to $\kappa_*X_0$; finally an assignment $\Xi$ sending a rigidified fake elliptic curve over an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, relative to $\psi\colon \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, to a $G$-point of $M$ over $B$, subject to four hypotheses: over connected $B$ the structural map of $\Xi(x)$ is a Frobenius twist $\mathrm{frobTwist}\,Fr^k\,\psi$; $\Xi$ is compatible with pullbacks along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; $\Xi$ is unchanged under an isomorphism of the underlying curves which is matched by the explicit compatibility of the rigidification data up to powers of $r$; and, over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, any formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve yields $j \le 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, transported from $(\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0)$ in the sense of `IsRigTransport`, with $\Xi(x) = \langle \mathrm{frobTwist}\,Fr^{-j}\,\psi, \eta(t)\rangle$. The conclusion: for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, and every $G$-point $y$ of $M$ over $k$, there are an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi\colon \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ and a pair $x$ consisting of a fake elliptic curve over $k$ together with a rigidification relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$, such that $\Xi(x) = y$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of Drinfeld's dictionary between rigidified fake elliptic curves and rigidified special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules, here on geometric points of the special fibre. It feeds the combined bijectivity statement over Artinian rings with algebraically closed residue field, which is the local comparison underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve.
